.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_CTX_GET0_PKEY 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_pkey ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_peerkey
.Nd functions for accessing the EVP_PKEY associated with an EVP_PKEY_CTX
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft EVP_PKEY *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_pkey
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_PKEY *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_peerkey
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_pkey
is used to access the
.Vt EVP_PKEY
associated with the given
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
.Fa ctx .
The
.Vt EVP_PKEY
obtained is the one used for creating the
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
using either
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey 3 .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_peerkey
is used to access the peer
.Vt EVP_PKEY
associated with the given
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
.Fa ctx .
The peer
.Vt EVP_PKEY
obtained is the one set using either
.Xr EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer_ex 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_pkey
returns the
.Vt EVP_PKEY
associated with the EVP_PKEY_CTX or NULL if it is not set.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_get0_peerkey
returns the peer
.Vt EVP_PKEY
associated with the EVP_PKEY_CTX or NULL if it is not set.
.Pp
The returned EVP_PKEY objects are owned by the EVP_PKEY_CTX, and
therefore should not explicitly be freed by the caller.
.Pp
These functions do not affect the EVP_PKEY reference count.
They merely act as getter functions, and should be treated as such.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer_ex 3
